      "writtenOn": "2022-03-30T12:21:15Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yeah it\u0027s debatable whether this will make a big difference, but that makes me a little nervous. Perhaps just add a separate iommu_lock? On the plus side, eventually this new lock should become a rwlock when we get support for them, and we could just take a write lock here and a read_lock when accessing the device llist from e.g. the mem abort path instead of relying on the host lock for serialisation. That\u0027s for later, but having a separate lock now shouldn\u0027t hurt. Thoughts?",
